        "firstMessage": {
          "author": {
            "displayName": "Yan Zhou",
            "tier": "EXPERT",
            "url": "/yanzhou06"
          },
          "content": "<p>Hi <a href=\"/yanyao23\" target=\"_blank\">@yanyao23</a> <a href=\"/martynaplomecka\" target=\"_blank\">@martynaplomecka</a> <a href=\"/ashleyoldacre\" target=\"_blank\">@ashleyoldacre</a> , thanks for organizing this competition!</p>\n<p>Any chance we could get more training data? 2,699 samples for 18 models feels like way too little.</p>\n<p>With more data, participants could focus more on building better solutions instead of wasting time and money generating tons of data. Otherwise, this might end up being more of a synthetic data competition.</p>\n<p>Of course, more data wouldn't make the competition perfectly fair. People with bigger budgets could still generate even more data, but at least it'd make spending money on synthetic data less important and give people with smaller budgets a real shot at winning.</p>\n<p>And I imagine generating more samples wouldn't be that hard for the organizers?</p>",
          "id": 3539714,
          "isThankYou": false,
          "postDate": "2026-10-16T11:18:22.127Z",
